{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463198",
      "title": "Working with Watchers",
      "lectureOrder": 32,
      "videoOrder": 28,
      "sourceHash": "35b13a2d358d6959a79b012081296fb65865d12d8284839f3b648ad16fa80e93",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "Now we learned about computed properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 7.92,
          "en": "a key feature for outputting dynamic values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.92,
          "end": 10.57,
          "en": "that depend on multiple input values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.57,
          "end": 13.8,
          "en": "or like in this case here on one input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.8,
          "end": 16.24,
          "en": "and one hard-coded value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.24,
          "end": 19.84,
          "en": "They're all this and never reactivity feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.84,
          "end": 23.79,
          "en": "built into Vue, and that would be watchers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.79,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "What are Watchers?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 29.02,
          "en": "Well, a watcher is basically a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.02,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "you can tell Vue to execute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 34.75,
          "en": "when one of its dependencies changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.75,
          "end": 37.67,
          "en": "Okay, that sounds just like computed properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.67,
          "end": 39.06,
          "en": "doesn't it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.06,
          "end": 41.43,
          "en": "Well, indeed you can use Watchers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.43,
          "end": 43.73,
          "en": "instead of computed properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.73,
          "end": 45.82,
          "en": "and here's how that would work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.82,
          "end": 47.973,
          "en": "and why you maybe don't wanna do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.9,
          "end": 53.9,
          "en": "Let me add a full name, data property here like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.21,
          "end": 57.44,
          "en": "and therefore let's comment out this full name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.44,
          "end": 60.91,
          "en": "computed property so that we don't have a name clash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.91,
          "end": 64.13,
          "en": "You don't wanna use a computed and a data property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.13,
          "end": 65.213,
          "en": "with the same name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 68.62,
          "en": "Now we can add a new configuration here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.62,
          "end": 72.52,
          "en": "a new option to this object we passed to create app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.52,
          "end": 75.85,
          "en": "again anywhere in their, position doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.85,
          "end": 77.17,
          "en": "I'll add it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.17,
          "end": 82.17,
          "en": "And that's the watch option just like data computed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.43,
          "end": 84.53,
          "en": "and methods, this name is not up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.53,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "it's one of the supported features Vue has,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 89.393,
          "en": "and therefore this has to be watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.35,
          "end": 94.96000000000001,
          "en": "Watch wants an object, just like computed and methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.96000000000001,
          "end": 96.34,
          "en": "And, and here again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.34,
          "end": 99.15,
          "en": "you'll define a bunch of methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.15,
          "end": 104.15,
          "en": "To be precise here, you can now use a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 107.9,
          "en": "you used in a data or computed property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.9,
          "end": 111.02000000000001,
          "en": "as a name for a watcher method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.02000000000001,
          "end": 111.85300000000001,
          "en": "For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.85300000000001,
          "end": 113.45,
          "en": "here we could use name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.45,
          "end": 115.75,
          "en": "because we have that name data property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.75,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "and define it as a method here in watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 120.22,
          "en": "Technically, this is okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.22,
          "end": 123.02,
          "en": "we'll not have any name clashes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.02,
          "end": 126.32,
          "en": "This tells Vue one important thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.32,
          "end": 131.32,
          "en": "Whenever name changes, this watcher method will re execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.32,
          "end": 135.15,
          "en": "and that's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.15,
          "end": 139.32999999999998,
          "en": "This name here being used here sets up this connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.32999999999998,
          "end": 140.82,
          "en": "That's how watchers work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.82,
          "end": 145.03,
          "en": "You repeat another data or computed property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.03,
          "end": 148,
          "en": "in a watcher method as a method name there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148,
          "end": 149.323,
          "en": "and when you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.323,
          "end": 154,
          "en": "that watcher method will be executed automatically by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154,
          "end": 157.44,
          "en": "whenever a property of that name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.44,
          "end": 161.25,
          "en": "so this case, whenever the name property changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 164.11,
          "en": "We could also watch the counter property instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.11,
          "end": 166.73,
          "en": "but here I wanna watch the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.73,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "And then in here we can specify any logic we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 173.29,
          "en": "We don't return anything because we're not going to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.29,
          "end": 178.09,
          "en": "the watcher anywhere in our HTML code to use a return value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.09,
          "end": 181.27,
          "en": "Instead in here we run logic that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.27,
          "end": 182.74,
          "en": "When the name changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.74,
          "end": 183.573,
          "en": "For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.573,
          "end": 185.947,
          "en": "we could update full name here, and set it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.947,
          "end": 190.023,
          "en": "= to this.name + an empty space + Schwartzmuller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.17,
          "end": 196.17000000000002,
          "en": "Actually, we don't even need to refer to this.name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.17000000000002,
          "end": 199.87,
          "en": "a watcher function automatically gets the last value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.87,
          "end": 204.53,
          "en": "the latest value of the watch property as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.53,
          "end": 206.98,
          "en": "This is passed in automatically by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.98,
          "end": 209.93,
          "en": "this latest value of the watch property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.93,
          "end": 212.05,
          "en": "Hence, we can accept it as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.05,
          "end": 214.94299999999998,
          "en": "name it however you want, and then use it in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.93,
          "end": 219.61,
          "en": "We actually also could accept a second argument here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.61,
          "end": 223.84,
          "en": "besides the value and that would then be the previous value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.84,
          "end": 226.59,
          "en": "the old value of the watch property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.59,
          "end": 228.06,
          "en": "Here I'm just accepting one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.06,
          "end": 229.71,
          "en": "because we only need that one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.71,
          "end": 233.06,
          "en": "but you could accept two arguments If you wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.06,
          "end": 235.113,
          "en": "New value and old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 239.21,
          "en": "And with that we would also update the full name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.21,
          "end": 241.33,
          "en": "whenever the name changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.33,
          "end": 244.57,
          "en": "If we save that and reload, indeed, if I type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.57,
          "end": 248.3,
          "en": "you have the same behavior as before with one difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.3,
          "end": 250.56,
          "en": "we always see Schwartz Muller here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.56,
          "end": 255.35,
          "en": "but we could also change this, check if value is empty...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.35,
          "end": 257.69,
          "en": "It's an empty string and if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.69,
          "end": 260.803,
          "en": "we set full name equal to an empty string as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.803,
          "end": 263.98,
          "en": "That would be how we could ensure that full name is empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.98,
          "end": 267.38,
          "en": "If value is empty, actually of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.38,
          "end": 270.33299999999997,
          "en": "I should then put the other code into an else block Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.49,
          "end": 274.173,
          "en": "and now we have that described behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.65999999999997,
          "end": 277.28,
          "en": "So that's a watcher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 277.28,
          "end": 278.113,
          "en": "And as you see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.113,
          "end": 281.523,
          "en": "you could use it as an alternative to a computed property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.37,
          "end": 284.11,
          "en": "Now we have a couple of problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 284.11,
          "end": 286.09000000000003,
          "en": "if we use it for that though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.09000000000003,
          "end": 286.923,
          "en": "for one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 286.923,
          "end": 289.79,
          "en": "I would argue that the concept of a computed property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 289.79,
          "end": 292.92,
          "en": "is maybe a bit easier to understand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 292.92,
          "end": 297.61,
          "en": "but the bigger problem arises If we have a computer property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 297.61,
          "end": 300.71,
          "en": "that would use more than one dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.71,
          "end": 304.54,
          "en": "let's say we have a second input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.54,
          "end": 306.68,
          "en": "I just duplicated my input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 306.68,
          "end": 309.403,
          "en": "and there we have a last name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 313.54,
          "en": "Now we add a new data property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 313.54,
          "end": 316.03,
          "en": "last name, which initially is an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.03,
          "end": 319.873,
          "en": "and this is bound with the model on that second input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 321.41,
          "end": 323.6,
          "en": "Now we have these two names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 323.6,
          "end": 327.79,
          "en": "Now we wanna update the full name whenever the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 327.79,
          "end": 329.963,
          "en": "or the last name changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 331,
          "end": 332.77,
          "en": "To achieve this with a watcher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.77,
          "end": 336.01,
          "en": "we need to add a second watcher because the first one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 336.01,
          "end": 338.103,
          "en": "simply watches the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 339.02,
          "end": 340.86,
          "en": "Now we need to add a second one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 340.86,
          "end": 345.48,
          "en": "where we also watch last name and get the value of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 345.48,
          "end": 349.3,
          "en": "And in here we have almost the same code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 349.3,
          "end": 351.697,
          "en": "but we wanna set the full name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 351.697,
          "end": 356.40999999999997,
          "en": "= to this.name + blank + lost + value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.18,
          "end": 362.32,
          "en": "because here we get the latest value of last name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.32,
          "end": 364.98,
          "en": "and up there in our first watcher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 364.98,
          "end": 369.43,
          "en": "we wanna change this to value + blank + this.last name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 369.43,
          "end": 371.65,
          "en": "because we're watching name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 371.65,
          "end": 376.65,
          "en": "Now we have two watchers to reflect the full name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 377.21,
          "end": 379.623,
          "en": "which is managed with two inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.64,
          "end": 383.86,
          "en": "And yes, this works, but it's a lot of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 383.86,
          "end": 387.12,
          "en": "especially if we compare it to the computed property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 387.12,
          "end": 388.85,
          "en": "alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 388.85,
          "end": 393.303,
          "en": "Let me comment out the full name, data property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.2,
          "end": 398.84000000000003,
          "en": "and let's also comment out the watchers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 398.84000000000003,
          "end": 400.13,
          "en": "We could remove them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 400.13,
          "end": 402.84000000000003,
          "en": "but I'll keep them around for reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 402.84000000000003,
          "end": 405.09000000000003,
          "en": "And let's bring back the computed property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 405.09000000000003,
          "end": 409.13,
          "en": "to see how much easier it is with a computed property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 409.13,
          "end": 412.81,
          "en": "There if we want to use two dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 412.81,
          "end": 416.67,
          "en": "we simply reference two dependencies like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
